.TH UNIM-POPUP-SERVICE 1 "August 2026" "UNIM 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-popup\-service \- UNIM popup rendering sidecar service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-popup\-service
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBunim-popup-service\fR is the dedicated popup rendering process for UNIM
(Universal Next-generation Input Method). It subscribes to the
\fBorg.atit.unim.Popup\fR D\-Bus interface and renders hanja, special-character,
and emoji popups as a GTK4 window.
.PP
In UNIM 0.3.0 this process is the single source of truth (SoT) for popup
state on X11 environments and Wayland desktops other than GNOME. On
GNOME Wayland, the GNOME Shell extension renders popups directly using
St widgets because Mutter does not support the wlr-layer-shell or
zwp_input_popup_v2 protocols required for GTK4 overlay windows.
.PP
The process is normally started automatically via D\-Bus session activation
(\fBorg.atit.unim.PopupService.service\fR). Manual launch is only needed for
debugging.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-daemon
Run in the foreground without daemonizing.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH D\-BUS INTERFACE
.TP
.B Service
org.atit.unim.PopupService
.TP
.B Object path
/org/atit/unim/popup
.TP
.B Interface
org.atit.unim.Popup
.PP
The interface exposes the following signals (forwarded from the daemon):
.TP
.B PopupRender
The single view\-model payload. Contains cells, header, footer, tabs,
highlight index, and pagination state. All renderers consume this signal
exclusively.
.TP
.B ShowHanjaPopup, ShowSpecialCharPopup, ShowEmojiPopupV2
Cursor\-coordinate trigger signals that inform the renderer where to
position the popup window.
.TP
.B HidePopup, CancelHanja, CancelSpecialChar
Dismiss signals. The popup\-service closes the GTK4 window on receipt.
.TP
.B HanjaBookmarkChanged, PopupNavigate
Navigation and bookmark signals. Each is accompanied by a PopupRender
re\-emission from the daemon.
.PP
To verify the interface is live:
.PP
.nf
busctl \-\-user introspect org.atit.unim.PopupService /org/atit/unim/popup
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UNIM_DEVELOP
Set to "1" to enable verbose debug logging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/dbus\-1/services/org.atit.unim.PopupService.service
Per-user D\-Bus activation file (installed by package or \fBmake install\fR).
.TP
.B /usr/share/dbus\-1/services/org.atit.unim.PopupService.service
System\-wide D\-Bus activation file.
.SH NOTES
.PP
KDE Plasma 5.x Wayland: the \fBgtk4\-layer\-shell\fR library required for
Wayland popup positioning is not available in the Ubuntu 24.04 (noble)
standard repositories. Popups will not appear on that configuration.
Use an X11 session or switch to GNOME as a workaround.
